msgid ""
"Migrating from one deployment per contest to a single multi-contest "
"deployment"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide is for setups that ran parallel exams with **two (or more) "
"copies** of this Docker deployment on the same machine, each with its own"
" database, ports and scoreboard (for example scoreboards on 8890 and 7890"
" behind different domains). After migrating, one deployment serves every "
"contest and each olympiad keeps its own scoreboard. See [multi-contest.md"
"](multi-contest.md) for day-to-day use."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Below, **stack A** is the deployment you keep and **stack B** the one you"
" retire. Run each command from that stack's directory."
msgstr ""

msgid "1. Back up everything"
msgstr ""

msgid "For each stack, while it is running:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you use an external database, run `pg_dump` against the URL in "
"`CMS_DB_URL` instead. Keep these files until the first exam on the new "
"setup has finished."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. Update stack A"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The database schema is updated automatically when the stack starts (the "
"`db-init` container adds the `ranking_groups` table and the new contest "
"columns). Existing contests start as **inactive** and without a ranking "
"group; nothing changes for contestants until you switch to "
"`CMS_CONTEST_ID=ALL`. Ranking groups also have hide and freeze windows "
"and a **Staff password**, configured on the group page (see [multi-"
"contest.md](multi-contest.md)). If stack A **already** runs with "
"`CMS_CONTEST_ID=ALL`, its contest list is empty right after the update: "
"tick **Active** on its contests in the Admin Web Server straight away. "
"Check `./logs.sh` for errors before continuing."
msgstr ""

msgid "3. Bring stack B's contests into stack A"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Check for name collisions first.** Usernames, team codes and contest "
"names must be unique across both databases. List the ones present in "
"both:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Repeat with `SELECT code FROM teams` and `SELECT name FROM contests`. If "
"the same person has an account in both stacks, import only one copy: when"
" exporting in stack B, leave users out, and add those participations in "
"stack A afterwards. Rename anything else that collides in stack B (from "
"its Admin Web Server) before exporting."
msgstr ""

msgid "In stack B: `./export.sh` and pick the contests to move."
msgstr ""

msgid "Copy the new `.zip` from stack B's `dumps/` into stack A's `dumps/`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In stack A: `./import.sh`, pick that file, and **do not** wipe the "
"database."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Every contest you import arrives **inactive** and without a ranking "
"group, whatever its state was in stack B (dumps made before this update "
"work the same way). Contestants can't see it, or log in to it, until you "
"switch it on in step 5; the importer prints a warning for each contest as"
" a reminder."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The one exception is a full restore, which is meant for bringing back a "
"backup and not for this migration: if you answer yes to \"Drop database "
"before importing?\" (`-d`), every contest keeps the **Active** flag "
"stored in the dump."
msgstr ""

msgid "4. Update stack A's `.env`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`CMS_CONTEST_ID=ALL`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`CMS_WORKER_COUNT`: at least the sum of what both stacks used."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nothing else needs to change: the scoreboard keeps `CMS_RWS_HTTP_PORT` "
"(for example 8890). Stack B's ports (for example 7890) are no longer "
"used."
msgstr ""

msgid "Apply it with `./restart.sh`."
msgstr ""

msgid "5. Configure the contests in the Admin Web Server"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Ranking groups:** create one per olympiad (for example `olim` and "
"`omips`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Each contest:** tick **Active** where needed and choose its ranking "
"group."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Ranking groups → Root ranking → Regenerate:** clears the old single-"
"contest scoreboard at `/`."
msgstr ""

msgid "6. Update the reverse proxy (on the server)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Each scoreboard domain now points at the same port plus its group:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Do the same for the other olympiad (`…:8890/olim/`), keep "
"`proxy_buffering off;`, and point every contestant domain at stack A's "
"Contest Web Server. Reload the proxy."
msgstr ""

msgid "7. Verify, then retire stack B"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each scoreboard domain shows only its own contests and updates live when "
"a test submission is scored."
msgstr ""

msgid "The contest list shows exactly the active contests."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Then stop stack B: `./down.sh` in its directory. Keep its volumes and the"
" backups until you are confident."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rolling back"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In stack A: set `CMS_CONTEST_ID` back to the previous contest id and "
"`./restart.sh`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In stack B: `./up.sh` (its data is untouched unless you deleted its "
"volumes)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Restore the previous reverse-proxy configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The new database columns are harmless to the old setup: with a single "
"contest id they are ignored. To get back the exact pre-migration "
"database, restore the `backup-*.sql` taken in step 1."
msgstr ""

